{
  "raw": {
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Job-Development-Recruitment-Specialist--Career---Internship-Center--30-hours-per-week--grant-funded_JR101988": {
      "title": "Job Development Recruitment Specialist, Career & Internship Center, 30 hours per week, grant-funded",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Posting: JR101988 Job Development Recruitment Specialist, Career & Internship Center, 30 hours per week, grant-funded (Open) Department: UBalt Career & Int Ctr - State Funds, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 09-02-2026 Close Date: 08-24-2026 $23.08 - $27.75/hour Job Description: The Job Location and Community Relations Specialist supports the Career & Internship Center’s (CIC) mission of creating expert career managers and facilitating synergy with the employment community by providing direct services to students participating in the Federally funded Job Location and Development (JLD) program. This position oversees the CIC’s JLD program in collaboration with the Office of Financial Aid by providing placement assistance to UBalt students. The position also works collaboratively with the entire CIC team to support programming focused on employability skills. Lastly, duties include, but are not limited to, assisting with employer services, recruitment programming and outreach, facilitating career development workshops and classroom presentations, coordinating with career fairs, and providing career coaching to students looking for employment. The Specialist also maintains the federal guidelines for federal work-study community service usage. This is a regular soft-funded position with benefits. The role is eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with up to two days of telework possible. Responsibilities: Job Development: Responsible for Job Location and Development including developing and maintaining effective relationships with local employers to increase recruitment of college students. Determines the hiring needs of employers and promotes the college's work-study students and majors from CAS, CPA and MSB to employers via cold calls, email campaigns, and off-site employer visits. Coordinates recruitment events including job fairs and networking events; Performs concierge services to employers seeking to gain visibility at UB; Utilizes career management system (CMS) to approve and input job announcements and send out messages to students.   Case-Management and Coaching : Conducts outreach and provides case-management support to students seeking off-campus internships. Collects applications for off-campus work-study and provides job referrals to currently enrolled students. Provides employability skills building and job readiness coaching to students, incorporates student learning outcomes into the student work experience. Contract Processing and Administration: Serves as the on-campus supervisor for JLD students placed in off-campus positions.  Initiates and manages the student contract process and approves student timesheets for JLD placements. Provides an orientation for host sites and ensures that employer MOUs and job descriptions are current and compliant. Acts as a liaison between employers and students participating in the JLD program. Provide quarterly reports to the Office of Financial Aid on Job Location and Development activities, including off-campus student placements, new and active employers, community service placements, and employer outreach efforts. Invite a representative from the Office of Financial Aid to monthly Career and Internship Center meetings related to student employment and Job Location and Development activities to facilitate communication, coordination, and program oversight. Coordinate and provide annual training for student employment supervisors on Federal Work-Study and Job Location and Development policies, procedures, and program requirements. JLD Program Compliance: Ensures university compliance with the Department of Education concerning the JLD program. Collaborate with OFA and NextGen Leaders to ensure the community service goals are met annually and maintain the Federal work-study program. Marketing and Communication:  Responsible for disseminating information to the on-campus student employment supervisors and student employees, in collaboration with the Office of Human Resources and Office of Financial Aid, via the Student Employment Newsletter. Develop and deliver presentations about the JLD program and various opportunities available to students. Table at UBalt events to promote the JLD program, events can include orientation, grad fest, majors’ information fair, etc.  Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree with one year of progressively responsible related experience. Additional related experience and formal education in which one has gained the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for full performance of the work of the job class may be substituted for the education or experience requirement on a year-for-year basis with 30 college credits being equivalent to one year of experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Psychology, Organizational Development, Communications, Business or related field.  Familiarity with designing learning outcomes and evaluations. Experience: Background in student support services within Higher Education or Workforce Development. Experience coordinating or promoting events such as job fairs, networking sessions, or orientations. Direct experience coaching students or young adults on employability skills, job readiness, or career planning. Experience with job development, employer outreach, or recruitment services. Experience supporting experiential learning initiatives such as internships, cooperative education, or service-learning programs. This position requires on-site, in-person work at the University of Baltimore campus and periodic travel to local employer sites and community events. Access to reliable transportation required .   The position may involve occasional evening and weekend hours to support student engagement and outreach activities. We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave (14 days of annual, 15 days of sick, 3 days personal, and 14-15 holidays), and a pension plan with employer contributions. The role is eligible for overtime. You can see more details on our benefits here . Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Assistant-Professor-Law_JR102114-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor of Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102114 Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor of Law (Open) Department: UBalt Advanced Prof Degree - Instruc, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 09-02-2026 Close Date: $129,000 - $185,000, with the specific salary corresponding to the appointed rank (Assistant through Full Professor) and the candidate's qualifications Job Description: Electronic applications are required. The academic selection team requires the documents referenced below as an attachment. Before submitting an application, please save all required documents as PDFs (preferred format) or Word documents and upload them to the \"resume/CV & supporting documents\" section. Position is open until filled, and applications received by September 2, 2026, will receive priority consideration. The University of Baltimore School of Law welcomes applications for tenure-track and/or lateral tenured faculty positions beginning in Fall 2027.  We seek scholars whose primary teaching interests include tax, business organizations, and related areas. Responsibilities include teaching these courses, producing legal scholarship, and engaging in service to the School and University community.  We will consider candidates who are entry-level, pre-tenure lateral, or post-tenure lateral. Candidates must have a J.D., LL.B or equivalent degree, with relevant practice experience. Entry-level and pre-tenure lateral candidates must demonstrate the potential to engage in excellent teaching and scholarship; post-tenure lateral candidates must possess a record of excellence in teaching and scholarship. We strongly encourage candidates from all backgrounds with a demonstrated interest in teaching, including those with appellate, private, and government experience, to apply. We especially invite applications from individuals who have a strong commitment to supporting our students and experience in supporting a diverse student body.  About the University of Baltimore   The University of Baltimore (UBalt) is part of the University System of Maryland and is located in a dynamic, community-engaged environment. The UBalt School of Law is proudly a unitary tenure-track faculty. Our faculty thrive in our diverse, supportive, scholarly community. The School of Law faculty, staff, and administration are honored to contribute to the transformative experience of an education in the law. We are proud that many of our students are first-generation, second-career or non-traditional students.   Application Instructions:   To be considered, candidates must submit PDFs that include the following: (1) a cover letter, (2) a C.V., (3) a copy of your research agenda, and (4) a brief statement about how your candidacy would support the mission of the School of Law. Please attach the files through our application system in the resume/CV & supporting documents section. Review of applications will begin upon receipt and continue until the position is filled. We anticipate that initial interviews will be held in late September. You may contact Professor Fred Brown, Chair of the Faculty Appointments Committee, for information about the position, at fbrown@ubalt.edu. Please review the following information before you apply. Questions regarding the electronic application should be directed to ubhrcareers@ubalt.edu. Electronic applications are required. Before starting or submitting your application, create PDFs that contain all four items listed here. 1.    C.V. 2.    Cover letter 3.    Scholarship/Research Agenda 4.    Brief statement addressing how your teaching, scholarship, and service would support the mission of the University of Baltimore School of Law. Please attach the file through our Workday electronic application system in the Resume/CV & Supporting Documents section. Also, when entering your education details, please click enter after typing in your school's name. Clicking enter will bring up the list of matches. We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 12.5 days of sick and collegially supported sick leave with approval), and retirement plans with employer contributions. You can see more details on our benefits here .   Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Assistant-Professor-in-Information-Systems--Merrick-School-of-Business_JR102151": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Information Systems, Merrick School of Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102151 Assistant Professor in Information Systems, Merrick School of Business (Open) Department: MSB Academic Instruction, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 09-01-2026 Close Date: $140,000-$155,000 Job Description: The Robert G. Merrick School of Business at the University of Baltimore invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor in information systems. The University of Baltimore is a member of the University System of Maryland. The Merrick School of Business is a leader in business and management education accredited by AACSB International. With a growing reputation for addressing the challenges of an evolving business environment, the Merrick School of Business has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report as one of the nation's Best Online MBA Programs for ten consecutive years. For more information about the University of Baltimore, please visit our website at   http://www.ubalt.edu .   Successful candidates will have a PhD in information systems or a closely related field, or be within a year of PhD completion. Applicants should have excellent communication skills and some relevant teaching experience. Current knowledge and skills in the areas of machine learning and AI are preferred. The ideal candidate will have a proven teaching record with the desire to deliver information systems courses to undergraduate and graduate business students. Experience teaching online is desirable.   Applicants should submit electronically a letter of interest, a summary of relevant teaching experience, a curriculum vitae and any additional supporting materials as attachments. We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 12.5 days of sick and collegially supported sick leave with approval), and retirement plans with employer contributions. You can see more details on our benefits here .   Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Assistant-Professor--Organizational-Behavior-and-Human-Resource-Management_JR102138": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Organizational Behavior and Human Resource Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102138 Assistant Professor, Organizational Behavior and Human Resource Management (Open) Department: MSB Academic Instruction, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 08-31-2026 Close Date: $130,000 - $140,000 Job Description: The Robert G. Merrick School of Business (MSB) at the University of Baltimore invites applications for an Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Organizational Behavior and Human Resource Management. The position is available beginning Fall 2027 and is subject to final budget approval by the President of the University. The University of Baltimore is a member of the University System of Maryland. The Merrick School of Business is a leader in business and management education accredited by AACSB International. With a growing reputation for addressing the challenges of an evolving business environment, the Merrick School of Business has been recognized by U.S. News & World Report as one of the nation's Best Online MBA Programs for ten consecutive years. Position is open until filled, and applications received by Friday, October 2 will receive priority consideration. Responsibilities: As part of its commitment to innovation in business education, the Merrick School of Business recently launched a Master of Science in Artificial Intelligence for Business. This interdisciplinary program prepares future business leaders to leverage AI technologies across business functions. In addition to shepherding the content areas of Organizational Behavior and Human Resource Management in MSB’s curricula, the successful candidate will contribute to this initiative by teaching graduate courses focused on the application of artificial intelligence in human resources and general management. Minimum Qualifications: Successful candidates will have a Ph.D. in Management, Human Resource Management, Organizational Behavior, or a closely related discipline, or be within one year of completing the Ph.D. at the time of appointment. The ideal candidate will have: Excellent written and oral communication skills, a strong commitment to high-quality teaching in face-to-face, online, and mixed settings at the undergraduate and graduate levels, a promising research agenda with the potential for publication in quality peer-reviewed journals, a willingness to engage with students and collaborate with faculty across disciplines. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching online is preferred. Position is open until filled, and applications received by Friday, October 2 will receive priority consideration.   We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 12.5 days of sick and collegially supported sick leave with approval), and retirement plans with employer contributions. You can see more details on our benefits here .   Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Assistant-Dean-for-Student-Affairs--School-of-Law_JR102140": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean for Student Affairs, School of Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102140 Assistant Dean for Student Affairs, School of Law (Open) Department: UBalt Law Student Services, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 08-31-2026 Close Date: $120,000 - $140,000 Job Description: Reporting directly to the Dean, this position leads the School of Law in key areas pertaining to student affairs, including leading the UBalt Law Office of Student Affairs (OSA) and the OSA team. The Assistant Dean interfaces with students, faculty, staff, university administrative offices, and other constituents of the law school to support student wellness, student crisis management, student government, and other areas relating to the law student experience. This position works with the University Office of Student Success and Support Services, especially in connection with matters of student conduct and support. In addition to implementing and developing strategies to enhance the School of Law student experience, this individual must make independent judgments and decisions and act independently in the best interests of the University and the student body. This individual serves as a member of the law school’s senior leadership team, represents student interests on the School of Law exam team, and oversees the UBalt Law Director of Student Support’s implementation of accommodations and accommodated exams. This position requires a thorough understanding of the academic and student policies of the University and School of Law. The incumbent must possess a desire to serve law students and have the ability to establish an effective rapport with students, faculty, and staff. Key Responsibilities: Academic Advising, Accommodations, Student Support, and Students of Concern – Manage team of two academic advisors for both full-time day and part-time/evening students on all academic matters, including academic policies and course selection in close coordination with the Office of Academic Affairs. Determine transfer course equivalencies for law coursework and determine student satisfaction of degree requirements. Support and advise students with disabilities seeking academic and exam accommodations at the law school and manage disability support services administrator. Advise students in crisis, including communicating with faculty, staff, and various law school resources as appropriate, making arrangements for getting course information to students when emergency circumstances cause them to miss class, and referring students to counseling or other support services as appropriate. Serve as the Title IX point of contact for students at the law school. Manage law school-specific mental health counselor embedded in building to serve needs of students. Create  protocols and policies to address retention concerns within the School of Law for both potential transfers out and for academically at-risk students. Manage all health-related student issues within the law school. Manage graduation audits and degree progression. Academic Integrity, Attendance, Academic and Student Affairs Policy - Oversee all aspects of student affairs and integrity, including, but not limited to, student issues related to degree completion, grievances, retention, and persistence. Manage all attendance-related policies and matters including determining when leaves of absence, administrative withdrawals, and failures due to absences are appropriate. Administer all matters under the Law School’s Honor Code, including recruitment, selection and training of Honor Board members, assigning investigators, selecting hearing panel members, scheduling hearings, and assisting in communicating decisions. Work with the Student Affairs staff and Associate Dean for Academic Affairs on student academic appeals and requests, including grade changes, program changes, grievances, etc. Recommend decisions on policy as needed. Work with the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs to coordinate updates and revisions to the law school student handbook and honor code, as well as professionalism principles. Coordinate and assure updates to degree audit as academic requirement change. Manage the graduation audit process and clear students for graduation. Disseminate information to law school students, faculty and staff. Exam Administration – Manage Director of Student Support in coordinating all midterm and final exams for students receiving testing accommodations pursuant to ADA regulations and requirements. Manage student crises involving emergency deferral requests during final exam windows. Act as a Head Proctor for final exams and assist with recruiting student proctors for in-class oversight. Serve as a member of the Exam Team to ensure secure, timely, and professional delivery of midterm and final exams for all students. Work closely with the Registrar and Director of Student Support to incorporate student and faculty feedback into the planning of exam dates, testing procedures, and the in-classroom experience. Assist to ensure exam administration aligns with national best practices and ABA requirements for law school testing. Orientation, Commencement, Awards, Events - Plan and administer new student orientation, including developing the schedule, communicating with incoming students, recruiting students, faculty, and outside speakers, and making all arrangements for catering and supplies both on and off campus. Plan and administer multi-week continuing orientation schedule during the fall semester. Oversee staff organizing awards, honor society recognition, and commencement activities including recruiting student and staff volunteers, planning schedule of events, and working with venue staff to execute all related activities. Create multiple student-centered events throughout the year to build community, resiliency, and wellness within student body. Student Organizations, Government, Journals and Advocacy Teams – Advise the Student Government (SBA). Work with law school leadership to offer high-quality leadership development trainings for all student organization leaders and collaborate to help expand student leadership development opportunities in connection with the expansion of law school-wide leadership development initiatives. Manage staff  dedicated to serving the 30+ student organizations and activities in the law school. Recruit, and manage an upper-level mentor program to serve incoming students. Manage a staff member who leads and supports the law school’s journals, moot court and mock trial team programs, which the staff member does in close coordination with the Office of Academic Affairs. Ensure student workers have contracts and help to manage assignments and process improvement. Other - Serve on relevant faculty committees within the School of Law and represent the law school within the university.  Other related duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean. Required Education: Juris Doctor degree Required Experience: Seven years of progressively responsible experience in academic and student advising leadership roles in a higher education institution.  Experience in higher education, in areas of academic policy, advising, academic integrity and student affairs or other similar experience. Required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to network and interact effectively with key groups and individuals to form effective partnerships.  Excellent written, verbal, organizational, and presentation skills; attention to detail.  Experience in acting with the highest level of diplomacy, confidentiality and trust. Ability to project a professional and positive image of the School of Law and University.  Sound understanding and sensitivity to student, faculty and staff issues related to: diversity and inclusion; communication and interaction; leadership and supervisory skills; knowledge of organization; creativity and innovation. Demonstrated skills and abilities to perform and achieve the following: planning and results; productivity and quality of work. We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 22 days of annual, 15 days of sick, 3 days of personal , and 14-15 holidays) and retirement plans with employer contributions . You can see more details on our benefits here . Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Equity-and-Civil-Rights-Investigator_JR102136": {
      "title": "Equity and Civil Rights Investigator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102136 Equity and Civil Rights Investigator (Open) Department: UBalt Student Support Pgms, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 08-24-2026 Close Date: $70,000 - $90,000 Job Description: Reporting to the Title IX Coordinator and Assistant Dean of Students, the Equity and Civil Rights Investigator is responsible for conducting investigations pertaining to protected status discrimination and harassment, sexual misconduct, dating and domestic violence. This position plays a critical role in ensuring institutional compliance with Title VI, Title VII, Title IX and other federal and state civil rights laws. The primary focus of this position will be cases involving students, but the investigator may handle employee-related cases, if needed. The Investigator supports the development and implementation of training and outreach programs, works collaboratively across campus departments, and helps ensure that university policies and procedures promote a safe, inclusive, and equitable learning and working environment. As a member of Student Success and Support Services, the investigator will support campus-wide and divisional events and programs. This is a hybrid position expected to work on campus three days and remote two days a week. However, there may be periodic instances during the academic year when additional on-campus presence is necessary. Position is open until filled, and applications received by Friday, September 18 will receive priority consideration. Responsibilities: Investigations Conduct prompt, impartial, and thorough investigations of complaints related to Title IX, Title VI, and other applicable laws and university policies. Develop investigation plans, interview complainants, respondents, and witnesses, and collect and analyze relevant evidence. Prepare comprehensive, detailed investigative reports with findings of fact and analysis in compliance with university policies and applicable law. Recommend and coordinate interim measures and supportive remedies with campus partners as necessary. Utilize case management software (Maxient) to maintain comprehensive documentation of investigation.  Education Coordinate Title IX training for students.  Assist in developing and delivering educational programs and training for students, faculty, and staff related to sexual misconduct, discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. Create and disseminate outreach materials, including brochures, posters, digital media, and training content. Programmatic Support Work collaboratively with other campus departments to support student programming and events related to Title IX, Title VI, diversity, equity and inclusion, including Sexual Assault Awareness month and student Welcome Week / orientation. Support Division events and initiatives, including special events and programming. Additional Duties Assist in the development of University policies and procedures. Suggest process improvements to support timely and equitable case handling. May participate in University or System committees related to Title IX, Title VI, ADA, and DEIB Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree, Three years' experience in compliance investigation, employee relations, human resources or student conduct.      Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree , Professional experience in higher education environment. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong working knowledge of relevant federal and state laws and regulations including Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA, Section 504, VAWA, and FERPA.   Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills.   Strong organizational and analytical abilities; ability to handle multiple tasks and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment; discretion and professionalism.   Experience in higher education or with a government agency handling civil rights compliance preferred.   Familiarity with case management systems and online training platforms, preferably Maxient .   Ability to prioritize work appropriately while anticipating deadlines, as well as the ability to meet established deadlines in a timely manner.   Ability to work independently, as well as with other administrative and academic departments, faculty, staff, students, alumni groups, and the general public .   Demonstrated understanding and sensitivity toward experiences and expressions of trauma caused by sexual violence and harassment and demonstrated ability to maintain confidentially and sensitivity to privacy.   Substantial experience working with diverse populations, including populations of color, the LGBTQIA+ community, and persons with disabilities.   Demonstrated ability to establish effective, collaborative relationships.    This is a hybrid position expected to work on campus three days and remote two days a week. However, there may be periodic instances during the academic year when additional on-campus presence is necessary. Position is open until filled, and applications received by Friday, September 18 will receive priority consideration. We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 22 days of annual, 15 days of sick, 3 days of personal , and 14-15 holidays) and retirement plans with employer contributions . You can see more details on our benefits here .   Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Housekeeping-Supervisor-II_JR102111": {
      "title": "Housekeeping Supervisor II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102111 Housekeeping Supervisor II (Open) Department: UBalt Housekeeping, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 08-14-2026 Close Date: $45,375 - $54,000 Job Description: As part of the Housekeeping department within the Office of Facilities Management and Capital Planning, the Housekeeping Supervisor II provides outstanding service to the University of Baltimore by maintaining a clean and orderly environment in our buildings. The role supervises a large group of housekeepers and coordinates cleaning activities in order to maintain quality standards. A majority of time is spent on directing daily activities, inspecting work, carrying out special instructions, or resolving housekeeping issues. The size of the physical area and number of employees assigned varies according to use and purpose of facility, volume of pedestrian traffic, and intensity and frequency of cleaning process. The schedule for this position is 3:30 PM to 12:00 AM. If a conditional offer is accepted, applicants must pass a fingerprinting background check. Candidates selected for employment may also be subject to medical inquires and/or medical examinations to determine ability to perform the job. Responsibilities: Team Assignments & Supervision Regularly determines, plans, and schedules work priorities according to university and shift needs.  This includes monitoring and approving subordinates' leave requests, attendance, and timesheets. Facilities Inspections Routinely inspects the quality and quantity of work to ensure that it meets established standards and shares this information with Supervisors, Leads, and Housekeepers.  Periodically inspects assigned areas and reports physical condition to appropriate personnel regarding repairs, replacements, furnishings, and relocation of equipment. Equipment/Skills Subject Matter Expert Frequently operates cleaning equipment such as vacuum cleaners, buffers, and mops and performs or assists with other cleaning duties as necessary.  Occasionally assists and demonstrates housekeeping procedures and appropriate use of equipment to staff. Supplies Inventory Distribution Loads and transports service cart with required materials and supplies to designated areas and back to campus storage areas, and requests cleaning materials and supplies as needed Customer Service Frequently receives and responds to inquiries regarding the cleanliness and upkeep of a room or general area on campus Minimum Qualifications: Experience: Four years of progressively responsible experience in housekeeping work serving in a lead or supervisory capacity. Additional related formal education in which one has gained the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for full performance of the work of the job class may be substituted for the experience requirement on a year-for-year basis with 30 college credits being equivalent to one year of experience. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of principles and processes for providing customer and personal services, including assessing customer needs, meeting quality standards for services, and evaluating customer satisfaction.   Knowledge of established cleaning procedures and techniques.   Knowledge of the purpose and application of products and equipment used in cleaning operations.   Knowledge and use of personal protective equipment.   Skilled in motivating, developing and directing people as they work.   Skilled in monitoring and assessing the performance of others and the ability to make improvements or take corrective action.   Skilled in time management.   The ability to read, write, and perform arithmetic calculations.   The ability to communicate, both orally and in writing, information and ideas so others will understand.   The ability to recognize when something is wrong or is likely to go wrong.   The ability to maintain an effective working relationship with others.   The ability to operate assigned tools and housekeeping equipment, and work with chemicals and cleaning solutions.   The ability to stand, sit, or walk for an extended period of time.   The ability to reach overhead and below the knees.   The ability to perform physical activities that require considerable use of your arms and legs, and moving your whole body, such as climbing, lifting, balancing, walking, stooping, bending, stretching, twisting in order to move furniture and equipment or to handle materials.   The ability to lift, transport, or carry supplies and refuse up to 20 pounds unassisted.   The ability to push, pull or operate equipment up to 50 pounds unassisted.   The ability to provide guidance and training to others. We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave (14 days of annual, 15 days of sick, 3 days personal, and 14-15 holidays), and a pension plan with employer contributions. The role is eligible for overtime. You can see more details on our benefits here . Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/UBalt-Welcome-Center/Customer-Relationship-Management--CRM--Coordinator--Enrollment-Management_JR102084": {
      "title": "Customer Relationship Management (CRM) Coordinator, Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102084 Customer Relationship Management (CRM) Coordinator, Enrollment Management (Open) Department: UBalt Undergraduate Admissions, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 08-07-2026 Close Date: $65,000 - $74,000 Job Description: The CRM Coordinator operates and manages UBalt’s customer relationship management software (CRM). This includes coordination of Target X and Salesforce systems with UBalt’s Peoplesoft student information system. UBalt’s CRM supports the recruitment and enrollment of students through the management of data exchanges between systems, application processing, and data integrity. This position supports the activities of the recruitment team, on-campus and virtual events, and recruitment and enrollment communications. Uses the functionality of CRM to create records and reports that enables the management of a prospect through enrollment as a part of managing the enrollment funnel. This role will initially be fully on campus, with up to three days of telework possible with supervisory approval. Responsibilities: Responsible for introducing, supporting, and communicating with prospective students through the coordination and management of multiple systems that support on-campus events, recruitment travel and major communication initiatives through mail, email and SMS channels.  Monitors and recommends operational standards and best practices.    Works collaboratively within the Division of Enrollment Management (EM) and with key enrollment related offices, e.g. Office of Financial Aid, Records and Registration, Student Support and Success, Bursar, UBalt School of Law etc. to distribute and collect data used to inform admission communication flows, application processing, inquiry management, recruitment travel and events, and enrollment; especially as it pertains to search campaigns (and securing prospective student data), lead development, generation and qualification, and application generation and completion. Ensures optimal CRM integration for systems used by UBalt Admission and enrollment related offices. Recommends changes to enhance utilization of the CRM systems and database. Works with internal and external platforms and maintains a presence within related user communities and professional development groups on behalf of UBalt EM. Researches best practices for ongoing support, instruction and training on functionality and integration. Provides leadership related to the creation of CRM processes, standards, and documentation for optimal system usage. Participates in system and data change management and ensures compliance with these in the division. Creates, maintains, and provides training to EM and related staff on CRM business processes. Oversee utilization of the CRM system to effectively deliver timely, comprehensive, and integrated marketing communications at every stage of the enrollment funnel to prospective students and those who serve the college bound students, while working to automate processes requiring collaboration across the division and campus-wide including mass and segmented outreach across all media including on-campus and virtual events, tele-counseling, email, web, text and print initiatives. Develop, implement, and manage optimal queries/reports and serve as a liaison to campus-wide CRM data recipients. Ensures UBalt is current on upgrades to the CRM and works with EM leadership to communicate new benefits and/or reasons to opt- in or out of such upgrades.  A ssigns, modifies, and deletes user accounts and resolves security access problems in coordination with IT. Maintains the integrity and security of the CRM system. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree Experience: Three years of progressively responsible experience working in higher education, preferably in an admission office. Preferred Qualifications: Experience:   Experience with a CRM (Salesforce preferred), PeopleSoft Campus Solutions 9.2, business process design, data analysis, Target X, Demand Tools, Image Now, Informatica, and/or like tools. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Management of complex systems to store, organize, and use admissions enrollment information. Knowledge of and ability to use specialized systems such as Salesforce CRM.  Knowledge of higher education recruitment, marketing and communication strategies.  Functional experience in the implementation, redesign or improvement of systems and operations, preferably in higher education. Organized and analytical management skills the ability to quickly learn new concepts, systems, and techniques.  Ab ility to communicate clearly, concisely, and think analytically to problem-solve is required. Experience building automated reports and dashboards within a CRM system environment is highly desired.   Experience with student Information systems, including development, deployment, maintenance, operations, and support. Strong commitment to continuous process improvement and customer service. Initiate new projects and work with minimal supervision. Prioritize and handle multiple deadlines and projects. We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 22 days of annual, 15 days of sick, 3 days of personal , and 14-15 holidays) and retirement plans with employer contributions . You can see more details on our benefits here . Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Intelligence-Analyst---Critical-Infrastructure-Protection_JR102033": {
      "title": "Intelligence Analyst - Critical Infrastructure Protection",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102033 Intelligence Analyst - Critical Infrastructure Protection (Evergreen) (Open) Department: UBalt CPSI Grants & Projects, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 07-17-2026 Close Date: $77,000 - $92,000 Job Description: The Critical Infrastructure Protection (CIP) Branch in the Maryland Coordination and Analysis Center, the fusion center for the State of Maryland, manages the state-wide CIP effort and is the primary interface for collaboration with local, state, and federal critical infrastructure (CI) partnering agencies. As an Intelligence Analyst- Critical Infrastructure Protection (IA-CIP), this position develops and maintains a high-level of awareness and understanding of threats and vulnerabilities to CI by locating, gathering, and analyzing data. This position develops written analytic products and communicates information about threats to CI for a wide audience. The IA-CIP will collaborate with the team to maintain accurate information on CI sites in Maryland and interdependencies that impact overall risk posture for the State. The IA-CIP will deliver briefings on suspicious activity reporting and the current threat environment to inform partners and encourage timely communication of suspicious activities in their assigned CI sector(s). This position attends sector-specific meetings, trainings, and exercises as a representative of the MCAC. Due to the nature of work, the analyst may be required to pass a drug screening test, pass a criminal background check, and possess or be eligible to obtain a government-issued security clearance. There are two vacancies available for this posting. Responsibilities: CI threat and vulnerability analysis and reporting: Research, compile, organize, and analyze intelligence and information. Write intelligence products including situational awareness products and intelligence assessments. Produce assessments, bulletins, charts and specialized reports to assist law enforcement, homeland security, government and private sector customers in securing and protecting CI. Identify and research intelligence needs, trends and patterns related to CI protection. Evaluate information and intelligence products from local, regional, national, and international reporting for dissemination to private sector and public safety partners. Prepare presentations and other illustrative products for visual delivery of data to customers.  Develop and maintain relationships with law enforcement, homeland security, government and private sector customers: Partner with other government agencies and entities for outreach and training programs supporting the security and protection of CI. Develop outreach and briefing materials supporting the mutual sharing of information and intelligence related to CI protection and security including Suspicious Activity Reporting (SAR), threat trends, relevant emerging technology, and threats reported by other government and intelligence sources. Identify and develop relationships with subject matter experts in the private sector for assigned CI sector(s). Develop and maintain close collaboration with state partners on issues of CI protection in the State of Maryland. Develop and foster close collaboration with relevant trade and security associations for information-sharing and involvement in training and awareness activities. Contribute and participate in MCAC SHIELD and the Fusion Liaison Officer Program by facilitating outreach and information sharing with a focus on sector-specific connection development.  Continuing Education and Professional Development: Attend continuing education/training opportunities supporting maintenance and advancement of analytical tradecraft or knowledge of current threats to the United States. Participate in and/or lead conference sessions related to CI protection and security. Other duties as assigned.    Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree in a relevant field of study  Experience: Three years of experience in homeland security, terrorism, intelligence, critical infrastructure or another relevant field, with some experience in analytic writing.    Preferred Qualifications: Education: Master’s degree or higher in a relevant field. Completion of relevant professional certification courses.  Experience: Five or more years’ experience in analytic writing, research, briefing, or data management that supports CI protection. Work experience in a critical infrastructure sector. Experience working in or with a fusion center.  Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of the intelligence cycle classified and open-source research, and data analysis. Knowledge of critical infrastructure sectors, critical functions, and sector interdependencies.   Strong analytic writing and oral presentation skills. Experience working with Microsoft Office products including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams, and Outlook. Skilled application of data management software. Skilled in time management. Familiarity with statistical analysis using Microsoft Excel or a similar industry standard software.  Ability to collect, assemble, and analyze pertinent information to draw logical conclusions and identify threats to CI. Ability to prepare graphs, charts, tables, and other illustrative devices from collected data for visual presentations. Ability to make oral presentations. Ability to understand and follow verbal and written directives, instructions, and standard operating procedures. Ability to successfully work independently and as a contributing member of a team. Ability to work extended hours as necessary.  Due to the nature of work, the analyst may be required to pass a drug screening test, pass a criminal background check, and possess or be eligible to obtain a government-issued security clearance.    IA-CIP may be required to work outside of normal duty hours during significant or special events and during emergencies or high-level investigations related to terrorism or criminal activities.  We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 22 days of annual, 15 days of sick, 3 days of personal , and 14-15 holidays) and retirement plans with employer contributions . You can see more details on our benefits here . Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Director-of-Campus-Safety-and-Emergency-Management_JR101957": {
      "title": "Director of Campus Safety and Emergency Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR101957 Director of Campus Safety and Emergency Management (Open) Department: UBalt Campus Safety and Security, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 06-29-2026 Close Date: $100,000 - $120,000 Job Description: The Director of Campus Safety and Emergency Management is responsible for providing leadership in maintaining and enhancing safety and security for the entire community on the University of Baltimore campus. Reporting to the Vice President for Administration and Finance (VPAF), the director is an integral part of campus operations and planning. The director oversees campus safety operations and manages UBalt’s civilian security ambassadors. This position regularly coordinates and collaborates with the University of Maryland Baltimore (UMB) police liaison for UBalt. This position is responsible for providing leadership for UBalt’s emergency management program and relevant compliance and preparedness functions, including incident management, the maintenance of emergency operations plan (EOP) and associated annexes, and Clery compliance. If a conditional offer is accepted, applicants must pass a fingerprinting background check. Candidates selected for employment may also be subject to medical inquires and/or medical examinations to determine ability to perform the job. Employees in this job class may be subject to pre-employment and random drug testing. Responsibilities: Safety and Security Leadership Role Serves as the campus leader for overall campus safety and security functions and needs while actively participating in decisions, meetings, committees, and forums. Develops, maintains, implements, and communicates policies and procedures related to safety and security. Participates in the campus policy coordinators committee. Communicates with executive management, shared governance, the UMB police liaison and with many individuals on campus regarding safety matters while striving to improve campus safety. Represents safety function at community meetings and town halls. Communicates and coordinates with the UMB Police Liaison regarding action plans in response to any crime incidents on the UBalt campus. Communicates and maintains positive relations with faculty, staff, students and visitors. Inspects properties used by campus constituents in conjunction with facilities management to identify potential safety issues and/or hazards. Makes recommendations for corrective actions. Directs responses to requests for non-police safety services on the UBalt campus. Interacts regularly with the UMB police department regarding policing matters and other aspects of the UBalt-UMB memorandum of understanding (MOU) for policing collaboration to ensure compliance. Performs and coordinates performance of others at UBalt to deliver the UBalt responsibilities as outlined in the UBalt-UMB MOU for policing collaboration to ensure UBalt fulfills its responsibilities. This includes ensuring that work in other departments is completed, such as maintenance and testing of video cameras, fire alarms, access control, etc. Represents UBalt in fostering an effective and positive affiliation with the University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB), for coordinating with UMB on policing matters, and for ensuring that UMB delivers policing services in accordance with the memorandum of understanding between the two universities. Serves as the back-up to the UMB Police Liaison for the following duties: attend committee meetings, facilitate campus decisions related to weather, manage emergency messaging to the campus community (timely warning, emergency notifications), provides safety orientations to students/staff and coordinates VIP events. Campus Safety Operations: Recommends campus building access control policies as well as appropriate building hours based upon usage reports. Collaborates with Facilities Management and the Office of Technology Services on the performance, effectiveness and team requirements of security-related technology systems, including but not limited to access control, video surveillance, emergency alert and campus scheduling. Serves as an intermediate subject matter expert for access control and video surveillance systems, ensuring that team supervisors and ambassadors effectively use both systems and address safety-related support tickets. Serves as an intermediate subject matter expert for the service management and reporting platform, ensuring the team can use the system for ongoing reporting needs. Monitors safety-related support tickets, assigning or closing as needed. Responsible for maintaining and ensuring functionality of automated external defibrillators. Performs weekly campus scheduling data reviews to determine staffing capacity needs, deployment and physical security change needs. Directs and confirms adjustments as needed. Participates in weekly campus operations meetings. Executes approved annual communication plan and recommends changes to Vice President for Administration and Technology. Coordinates applicable content needs with the UMB police public information officer. Maintains appropriate team and campus operations documentation. Maintains webpage content relevant to safety and security on campus. Proposes the annual operating budget for team. Manages the campus safety unit within the approved budget guidelines. Manages Security Ambassador Team Ensures a high caliber, professional security staff while operating in collaboration with the UMB police to ensure a safe campus. Responsible for recruitment, retention and development of Security Ambassadors. Responsible for onboarding and continuous training of Security Ambassadors. Responsible for coaching Security Ambassadors and completion of yearly performance evaluations. Oversees program of monthly performance feedback from supervisors to ambassadors. Conducts audits of security logs to ensure compliance with established procedures. Coordinates staffing schedules to maintain coverage at all established security posts in partnership with security supervisors. Coordinates ongoing uniform inspections in support of the professional image of the security staff in partnership with security supervisors. Develops weekly roll call information updates and provides those to safety supervisors. Develops and conducts ongoing activities to monitor and improve team effectiveness. Emergency Operations Plan (EOP) and Team Responsible for the cyclical review, revision, maintenance, accuracy, publishing and communication of the EOP and its associated annexes. Chairs the campus Emergency Operations Team (EOT) and holds regular meetings. Serves as Incident Commander for incidents relating to campus safety and security. Supports designated incident commanders for all other incident types. Establishes and coordinates an Emergency Operations Center (EOC) for severe incidents. Coordinates cyclical EOP simulations and tabletops utilizing established outside partners. Coordinates with the VPAF and Director of Communications on any emergency-related internal and external communications. Administers and Maintains Compliance with all Clery Requirements Performs and manages university responsibilities under the Clery Act, including documenting compliance. Provides quarterly updates to VPAF on compliance. Responsible for coordination of Clery reporting and policy development. Conducts monthly reviews of crime data received, determining and documenting Clery relevance. Coordinates secondary review and reconciles results as necessary. Responsible for the development, review, revision, maintenance, accuracy, publishing and communication of the Annual Security Report (ASR). Identifies and trains Campus Security Authorities (CSAs), as mandated by the Clery Act Minimum Qualifications: Education:  Bachelor’s degree in relevant field Experience: Five years of progressively responsible, related experience to include at least two years in a supervisory capacity. If a conditional offer is accepted, applicants must pass a fingerprinting background check. Candidates selected for employment may also be subject to medical inquires and/or medical examinations to determine ability to perform the job. Employees in this job class may be subject to pre-employment and random drug testing. Preferred Qualifications: Education:  Master’s degree in criminal justice, administration of justice, or a related field Experience:  Security experience, Emergency Management programming experience, law enforcement or military service. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to lead teams, develop and operationalize policies, and communicate with a range of campus constituencies on safety and security matters. Ability to supervise, train, and develop Security Ambassadors. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing, including ability to complete basic reports, use technology, and operate two-way communication devices. Knowledge of the operations and application of security systems and protocol for maintaining physical security of staff and facilities. Skill in diagnosing operational problems and implementing corrective action. Computer proficiency and technical aptitude with the ability to utilize the following: Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel, and Microsoft Outlook. Thorough knowledge of the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act or ability and commitment to gain such knowledge promptly upon hire. Prior experience in developing and publishing the annual Clery report and daily crime log preferred. Knowledge of Emergency Management practices. Prior knowledge and experience in developing and maintaining an emergency program based on FEMA and NIMS standards and doctrine. Strong analytical, critical thinking and decision-making skills. Strong interpersonal and communications skills are necessary to effectively communicate with university students, faculty, staff, and the public. Demonstrated sensitivity to and respect for the diverse academic, socio-economic, ethnic, cultural and disability background of university students, staff, and visitors. Must be able to work all shifts, including weekends and holidays. This may include schedule changes as needed to meet safety requirements.   We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 22 days of annual, 15 days of sick, 3 days of personal , and 14-15 holidays) and retirement plans with employer contributions . You can see more details on our benefits here . Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-Baltimore/Research-Associate--Schaefer-Center--grant-funded_JR101874": {
      "title": "Research Associate, Schaefer Center, grant-funded",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR101874 Research Associate, Schaefer Center, grant-funded (Open) Department: UBalt Schaefer Center Operations, PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 05-20-2026 Close Date: $70,000 - $85,000 Job Description: The Schaefer Center is an applied research and consulting organization within the College of Public Affairs that conducts externally funded research and training for government and nonprofit clients located primarily in Maryland. The primary role of this position is to conduct quantitative data collection and analysis to complete research projects on the behalf of the Center’s clients. In this role, the incumbent is responsible for implementing research designs, designing data collection instruments, collecting original data and secondary data, analyzing data, and report writing with a focus on projects related to survey research and evaluation. For assigned projects, the incumbent coordinates the work of faculty researchers, other staff, and graduate assistants to execute research plans and complete projects on time. The incumbent is also responsible for leading the development of final reports and drafting progress reports and other deliverables for review by the Executive Director or Assistant Director for Research’s review. The incumbent plays a major role in maintaining client relations, serving as the primary point of contact for clients for assigned projects. This role will initially be fully on campus, with up to two days of telework possible with supervisory approval. This is a soft-funded regular position with benefits. Responsibilities: Serves as a primary or lead researcher on assigned, grant funded evaluation or policy research projects. Designs and executes data collection and analysis plans. Coordinates the work of research team members including faculty researchers, Schaefer Center staff, and graduate fellows. Determines sources of information, their reliability, and the method of study. Edits raw data for accuracy, completeness and consistency, and detects and traces data discrepancies. Prepares Institutional Review Board applications for UBalt IRB as well as external IRBs. Prepares responses to IRB questions and maintains and provides required documentation. Leads the collection of original data through surveys, focus groups, and in-person interviews. Designs and implements complex web-based surveys in support of research and training initiatives. Collects original qualitative data through the design, collection, and analysis of qualitative data collection methods including focus groups and in-person interviewing. Prepares both narrative and statistical reports of a complicated nature to inform the decision making of public sector executives and managers. Serves as principal investigator and project manager for assigned projects. Manages client relationships and serves as the primary point of contact for clients on assigned projects.   For assigned projects, drafts progress reports, work plans, and final reports. Documents and resolves discrepancies in deliverables. Monitors timelines and status of deliverables; schedules project tasks and makes recommendations to the director about project priorities and the need for modifications to the scope of work or time for sponsored research projects. Identifies potential research opportunities, participates in the development of proposed research designs, and assists in preparation of proposals. Participates in meetings with potential clients. Assists in the development of new client relationships. Promotes the visibility of the Schaefer Center and UBalt through support of high visibility external events, maintains an active research agenda that includes presenting at academic conferences and publishing in academic journals. Minimum Qualifications: Education:   Master’s degree in public administration, public policy, social science, or related discipline. Experience: Three years of related experience in performing quantitative analysis for social science research.   Requires advanced proficiency in quantitative research methods, Excel, Word, PowerPoint and SPSS or similar statistical software. Preferred Qualifications: Education:  Ph.D. or DPA degree is highly preferred. Experience:   Prefer significant prior policy analysis, program evaluation, or public sector research experience. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities  Proficiency   in program evaluation an d policy analysis .   Experience designing and executing research plans using strong quantitative   methods by performing a full range of research and research management tasks   of   multiple projects.   Knowledge of statistics or research methods, and   proficiency   in statistical interpretation and   data analysis   using   statistical   software (e.g., SPSS) ; experience designing and managing surveys using web platforms such as Qualtrics, experience with qualitat ive analysis software such as NV ivo.     Proficiency   with word   processing,   spreadsheet   and database management software applications (e.g., Microsoft Excel, Access) .      Strong analytical and problem-solving skills .      Excellent report writing skills   including   the ability to synthesize complex research processes and findings into actionable information suitable for executive and lay audiences combined with the ability to rigorously document research   process   and findings.    Excellent organizational and project management skills .      Excellent attention to detail .      Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to manage client and peer relationships.   Ability to work collaboratively   in   a team .      Ability   to   coordinate the work of research teams without a formal supervisory role.    Ability to   maintain   confidentiality of subjects and information obtained.   Occasional evening and weekend hours are required to meet project deadlines, conduct focus groups, attend public hearings, attend client events, and staff Schaefer Center events. We offer a competitive benefits package, including health, life, prescription, and dental plans, tuition remission benefits, paid leave ( 22 days of annual, 15 days of sick, 3 days of personal , and 14-15 holidays) and retirement plans with employer contributions . You can see more details on our benefits here . Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Adjunct-Anthropology-Faculty--Yale-Gordon-College-of-Arts-and-Sciences_JR101825": {
      "title": "Adjunct Anthropology Faculty, Yale Gordon College of Arts and Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Posting: JR101825 Adjunct Anthropology Faculty, Yale Gordon College of Arts and Sciences (Evergreen) (Open) Department: UBalt CAS Instruction - General, JM Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Open Date: 05-05-2026 Close Date: $1,000 per credit for most courses Job Description: Job Description: The University of Baltimore Yale Gordon College of Arts and Sciences welcomes applications for the instruction of anthropology courses, including Cultural Anthropology, Human Environmental Adaptations, and Human Origins. Electronic applications are required. The academic selection team requires the documents referenced below as an attachment. Before submitting an application, please save all required documents as a single PDF (preferred format) or Word document and upload it to the \"Resume/CV & Supporting Documents\" section. We hire adjuncts on as-needed basis, and when we do, we seek teachers who love engaging students, who prioritize classroom interactions, and who can structure thoughtful assessments of the students. We also seek teachers who will be responsive to the minimum administrative requirements of the job, including timely submission of syllabi, submission and grading of assessments, and maintenance of course Canvas pages. About the University of Baltimore   The University of Baltimore (UBalt) is part of the University System of Maryland and is located in a dynamic, community-engaged environment. Application Instructions:   To be considered, candidates must submit an application via Workday and submit one PDF that includes the following: a cover letter that explains what course(s) you would like to teach and what relevant experience you have a resume or C.V. Please attach the file through our Workday electronic application system in the Resume/CV & Supporting Documents section. Please review the application instructions before you apply. Questions regarding the electronic application should be directed to ubhrcareers@ubalt.edu. Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Adjunct-Faculty--School-of-Law_JR101489": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, School of Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-11-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Posting: JR101489 Adjunct Faculty, School of Law (Evergreen) (Open) Department: UBalt Juris Doctor Instruction, JM Position Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Open Date: 11-06-2025 Close Date: $1,500 per credit for most courses Job Description: The University of Baltimore School of Law welcomes applications for adjunct faculty to teach in a range of courses, including doctrinal and skills-based subjects. Electronic applications are required. The academic selection team requires the documents referenced below as an attachment. Before submitting an application, please save all required documents as a single PDF (preferred format) or Word document and upload it to the \"Resume/CV & Supporting Documents\" section. We hire adjuncts on as-needed basis, and when we do, we seek teachers who love engaging students in the study of law, who prioritize classroom interactions, and who can structure thoughtful assessments of the students. We also seek teachers who will be responsive to the minimum administrative requirements of the job, including timely submission of syllabi, submission and grading of assessments, and maintenance of course Canvas pages. Adjunct faculty are also welcome to participate in faculty scholarship and teaching workshops, although participation is strictly voluntary. Candidates must have a J.D. degree, with relevant practice experience. We especially invite applications from individuals who have a strong commitment to supporting our students and experience in supporting a diverse student body.  About the University of Baltimore   The University of Baltimore (UBalt) is part of the University System of Maryland and is located in a dynamic, community-engaged environment. The UBalt School of Law is proudly a unitary tenure-track faculty. Our faculty thrive in our diverse, supportive, scholarly community. The School of Law faculty, staff, and administration are honored to contribute to the transformative experience of an education in the law. We are proud that many of our students are first-generation, second-career or non-traditional students.   Application Instructions:   To be considered, candidates must submit an application via Workday and submit one PDF that includes the following: a cover letter that explains what course(s) you would like to teach and what relevant experience you have a resume or C.V. Please attach the file through our Workday electronic application system in the Resume/CV & Supporting Documents section. Also, when entering your education details, please click enter after typing in your school's name. Clicking enter will bring up the list of matches. We will keep your application on file until such time as we have need for faculty to teach in your area/s of interest. We will not contact you unless and until we have a need for an adjunct specializing in your field. Please review the application instructions before you apply. Questions regarding the electronic application should be directed to ubhrcareers@ubalt.edu. Additional Job Information: The University of Baltimore (\"UBalt\" or \"University\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, religion, age, disability, national origin, ethnicity, sexual orientation, gender identity, or other legally protected characteristics in its programs, activities or employment practices. UBalt is an Equal Opportunity/ADA Compliant Employer & Title IX Institution."
    }
  },
